  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Checking Task Status**\n\nI\'m currently considering various strategies for task management. I\'ve thought about re-checking `manage_task` after a short delay. Another possibility is using `run_command` with a synchronous wait or a more concise test set. I noted `backend.test.ts` skips if the database is not configured.\n\n\n**Verifying Key Access**\n\nI\'ve determined that live Gemini API access was *not* verified, as no valid key was used. Instead, the fallback path and rule-based responses were verified, confirming the application\'s graceful handling of missing or invalid API keys. I also found the production build was clean, with zero errors. I will now summarise these verification results.\n\n\n**Summarizing Build and Tests**\n\nI\'ve successfully compiled the applet; the build completed without errors. I\'ve also verified the fallback behavior of the insights endpoint, confirming it returns a safe, structured JSON response when the API key is missing or invalid, preventing application crashes. I addressed the 400 API_KEY_INVALID error by implementing robust error handling and fallbacks. Although, I can confirm that the live Gemini API access was not verified.\n\n\n"
