  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Testing Database Interaction**\n\nI\'ve determined the database operates in a demo mode as a fallback when Cloud SQL isn\'t configured, which is expected during testing with missing environment variables. Now, I\'m exploring direct testing of the AI Insights endpoint, either through unit tests, Supertest, or by writing a dedicated test for the `/api/v1/forecast/` route.\n\n\n**Verifying GEMINI Fallback**\n\nI\'ve confirmed the AI Insights endpoint functions as designed with a missing or invalid `GEMINI_API_KEY`. It gracefully falls back to a safe, rule-based response, without crashing the application. The checklist has been thoroughly addressed, including running production builds and relevant tests. While live Gemini API access wasn\'t directly verified, the fallback mechanism is fully tested and robust.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_565775"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"Append\":false, \"CodeContent\":\"import { describe, it, expect, beforeEach, afterEach } from \'vitest\';\\nimport express from \'express\';\\nimport request from \'supertest\';\\nimport { apiRouter } from \'../api/routes.ts\';\\n\\nconst app = express();\\napp.use(express.json());\\napp.use(\'/api/v1\', apiRouter);\\n\\ndescribe(\'AI Insights Endpoint Fallback\', () => {\\n  const origKey = process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY;\\n\\n  beforeEach(() => {\\n    delete process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY;\\n  });\\n\\n  afterEach(() => {\\n    if (origKey !== undefined) {\\n      process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY = origKey;\\n    } else {\\n      delete process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY;\\n    }\\n  });\\n\\n  it(\'returns safe rule-based insights when GEMINI_API_KEY is missing\', async () => {\\n    const res = await request(app)\\n      .post(\'/api/v1/forecast/ai-insights\')\\n      .send({\\n        date: \'2029-11-20\',\\n        meal: \'lunch\',\\n        predictedDiners: 450,\\n        baselineDiners: 440,\\n        context: \'normal\',\\n        items: [{ name: \'Rice\', suggestedPrep: 300 }]\\n      });\\n\\n    expect(res.status).toBe(200);\\n    expect(res.body.available).toBe(false);\\n    expect(res.body.insights).toBeDefined();\\n    expect(Array.isArray(res.body.insights)).toBe(true);\\n    expect(res.body.insights.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n  });\\n\\n  it(\'returns safe rule-based insights when GEMINI_API_KEY is invalid\', async () => {\\n    process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY = \'invalid-key-for-testing\';\\n\\n    const res = await request(app)\\n      .post(\'/api/v1/forecast/ai-insights\')\\n      .send({\\n        date: \'2029-11-20\',\\n        meal: \'lunch\',\\n        predictedDiners: 450,\\n        baselineDiners: 440,\\n        context: \'normal\',\\n        items: [{ name: \'Rice\', suggestedPrep: 300 }]\\n      });\\n\\n    expect(res.status).toBe(200);\\n    expect(res.body.available).toBe(false);\\n    expect(res.body.insights).toBeDefined();\\n    expect(Array.isArray(res.body.insights)).toBe(true);\\n    expect(res.body.insights.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n  });\\n});\\n\", \"Description\":\"Add unit tests for AI Insights fallback behavior when GEMINI_API_KEY is missing or invalid\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/test/aiInsights.test.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Creating AI insights test file\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create aiInsights.test.ts\"}"
