  planner_response {
    response: "### SMARTMESS AI \342\200\224 FINAL HACKATHON DELIVERY REPORT\n\nWe have successfully completed all priorities and verified the application codebase, production build, and test suite.\n\n---\n\n### Summary of Completed Priorities & Deliverables\n\n1. **Redesigned Login Experience (Priority 1)**:\n   - Transformed the sign-in page into a polished AI SaaS landing screen featuring a deep navy background (`#0a0f1d`), emerald-green accents, and glowing ambient gradients.\n   - Added the brand subtitle: *\"AI-powered institutional dining intelligence\"* and headline: *\"Transforming Institutional Kitchens Through Smart Demand Forecasting & Waste Prevention\"*.\n   - Included a product preview metrics grid highlighting Demand Forecasting, AI Assistant & Insights, and Waste Reduction Analytics.\n   - Upgraded role selector cards for **Mess Manager**, **Kitchen Staff**, and **Student/Diner** with clear synthetic profile labeling and one-click demo sign-in.\n\n2. **Full Conversational AI Assistant (Priority 2)**:\n   - Added **AI Assistant** to the navigation sidebar for all role personas.\n   - Built a polished chat interface (`src/pages/AiAssistant.tsx`) with message bubbles, timestamps, loading indicators, clear chat action, and **8 clickable suggested prompts** covering waste totals, period comparisons, top leftover dishes, attendance trends, prep targets, and practical waste reduction advice.\n   - Implemented a secure backend Express endpoint (`POST /api/v1/chat`) in `src/api/routes.ts` that safely computes data-aware metrics (residual waste quantities, top surplus dishes, average attendance, and approved preparation targets) from actual records.\n   - Integrated server-side `@google/genai` (`gemini-3.8-flash`) with robust rule-based fallback when `GEMINI_API_KEY` is unconfigured.\n\n3. **End-to-End Workflow & Notifications (Priority 3)**:\n   - Verified the complete approval-to-notification sequence: Manager plan approval generates a student notification with an unread badge counter and direct link to the approved menu, while synchronizing approved prep targets for Kitchen Staff.\n   - Role-based access control (RBAC) strictly enforces permissions across Manager, Kitchen Staff, and Student tokens.\n\n4. **Forecasting Credibility & Methods (Priority 4)**:\n   - Maintained transparent, deterministic rule-based demand forecasting incorporating day-of-week patterns, recent trends, menu composition effects, and special campus context without unsupported claims.\n\n5. **n8n Automation Status (Priority 5)**:\n   - Explicitly disclosed as unconfigured / not connected in settings and status documentation.\n\n6. **Build, Test, & Finishing (Priority 6)**:\n   - **TypeScript Compilation (`tsc --noEmit`)**: PASSED (0 errors).\n   - **Linting & Production Build (`npm run build`)**: PASSED (Vite production bundle built cleanly).\n   - **Test Suite (`npx vitest run`)**: All hackathon feature tests, workflow checks, and fallback unit tests passed successfully.\n   - Updated `TASK_STATUS.md` with complete documentation."
    thinking: "**Evaluating Implementation Success**\n\nI\'m pleased to report a successful build! Now, I\'m carefully reviewing the implementation to ensure it meets every requirement outlined in the user request. So far, the focus is on the crucial redesign of the login experience, where I\'m cross-checking the deep navy background, the emerald-green accents, and the high-contrast text to meet the target requirements.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "### SMARTMESS AI \342\200\224 FINAL HACKATHON DELIVERY REPORT\n\nWe have successfully completed all priorities and verified the application codebase, production build, and test suite.\n\n---\n\n### Summary of Completed Priorities & Deliverables\n\n1. **Redesigned Login Experience (Priority 1)**:\n   - Transformed the sign-in page into a polished AI SaaS landing screen featuring a deep navy background (`#0a0f1d`), emerald-green accents, and glowing ambient gradients.\n   - Added the brand subtitle: *\"AI-powered institutional dining intelligence\"* and headline: *\"Transforming Institutional Kitchens Through Smart Demand Forecasting & Waste Prevention\"*.\n   - Included a product preview metrics grid highlighting Demand Forecasting, AI Assistant & Insights, and Waste Reduction Analytics.\n   - Upgraded role selector cards for **Mess Manager**, **Kitchen Staff**, and **Student/Diner** with clear synthetic profile labeling and one-click demo sign-in.\n\n2. **Full Conversational AI Assistant (Priority 2)**:\n   - Added **AI Assistant** to the navigation sidebar for all role personas.\n   - Built a polished chat interface (`src/pages/AiAssistant.tsx`) with message bubbles, timestamps, loading indicators, clear chat action, and **8 clickable suggested prompts** covering waste totals, period comparisons, top leftover dishes, attendance trends, prep targets, and practical waste reduction advice.\n   - Implemented a secure backend Express endpoint (`POST /api/v1/chat`) in `src/api/routes.ts` that safely computes data-aware metrics (residual waste quantities, top surplus dishes, average attendance, and approved preparation targets) from actual records.\n   - Integrated server-side `@google/genai` (`gemini-3.8-flash`) with robust rule-based fallback when `GEMINI_API_KEY` is unconfigured.\n\n3. **End-to-End Workflow & Notifications (Priority 3)**:\n   - Verified the complete approval-to-notification sequence: Manager plan approval generates a student notification with an unread badge counter and direct link to the approved menu, while synchronizing approved prep targets for Kitchen Staff.\n   - Role-based access control (RBAC) strictly enforces permissions across Manager, Kitchen Staff, and Student tokens.\n\n4. **Forecasting Credibility & Methods (Priority 4)**:\n   - Maintained transparent, deterministic rule-based demand forecasting incorporating day-of-week patterns, recent trends, menu composition effects, and special campus context without unsupported claims.\n\n5. **n8n Automation Status (Priority 5)**:\n   - Explicitly disclosed as unconfigured / not connected in settings and status documentation.\n\n6. **Build, Test, & Finishing (Priority 6)**:\n   - **TypeScript Compilation (`tsc --noEmit`)**: PASSED (0 errors).\n   - **Linting & Production Build (`npm run build`)**: PASSED (Vite production bundle built cleanly).\n   - **Test Suite (`npx vitest run`)**: All hackathon feature tests, workflow checks, and fallback unit tests passed successfully.\n   - Updated `TASK_STATUS.md` with complete documentation."
    thinking_duration {
