  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Token Handling**\n\nI\'ve been examining the `switchRole` function and its use of fallback tokens. Specifically, I\'m focusing on how `auth.ts` handles those tokens. I\'ve pinpointed the relevant code block within `src/middleware/auth.ts`, the one that explicitly addresses verified demo/test tokens, which has provided additional context to the flow.\n\n\n**Investigating Demo Token Flow**\n\nI\'m now diving deeper into how the system verifies and utilizes demo tokens, particularly focusing on the `DEMO_TOKENS` object and its interaction with the database. The code checks for tokens in a dictionary before hitting the database. I\'m exploring the specific error handling scenarios, such as when the database lookup fails or if the user isn\'t found, and the implications of these failure points.\n\n\n**Clarifying Unconfigured Database Handling**\n\nI\'ve discovered the `getUserByUid` function throws a `DatabaseConfigurationError` when the database is unconfigured, as `isConfigError` is true. `auth.ts` then returns a 503 error, even for demo tokens, which seems wrong. I\'m focusing on why `requireAuth` doesn\'t fall back to a demo user in that scenario. The `DEMO_TOKENS` mapping shows the demo user UIDs; now I\'m thinking about what `req.user` and `req.userRole` should be when the database is unavailable but a demo token is provided.\n\n\n**Refining Demo Token Fallback**\n\nI\'ve clarified the demo token role assignment logic, mapping specific tokens to roles like \'manager\', \'kitchen_staff\', and \'student\'. I\'m now working to integrate a fallback mechanism where, during a database configuration error, the system defaults to a synthetic demo user if a demo token is present, preventing unnecessary 503 errors and allowing demo access. This seems like a good solution.\n\n\n**Addressing Session Authentication**\n\nI\'ve shifted my attention to `src/api/routes.ts`, specifically the `POST /auth/session` route. It also returns a 503 error when the database is unconfigured. I\'m now comparing the demo token handling between this route and the `requireAuth` middleware. This route, similar to the middleware, doesn\'t fall back to a demo session when `isConfigError` is true. I am thinking this is an important area for improvement.\n\n\n**Implementing Demo Data Fallback**\n\nI\'ve examined the `POST /api/v1/chat` route and noticed it handles database errors by returning empty record lists, then from that it uses the `createSeedState()` function in `src/data/mockData.ts` to provide operational data. I\'ve concluded it\'s an important area for demonstration and user experience when the database is unconfigured.\n\n\n**Evaluating Data Integration**\n\nI\'m now thinking about how to integrate the mock data from `createSeedState().records`, and how the assistant can use this data when the database is unavailable. I\'m focusing on calculating specific metrics like total food waste over the last 30 days and average attendance, and preparing current approved preparation targets to provide a useful demo experience.\n\nI\'ve also encountered a client error: `SyntaxError: Unexpected token \'<\', \"<!doctype \"... is not valid JSON` and I\'m tracing the cause. I\'ve narrowed it down by examining `apiClient.ts` to see what is going on with the request from the browser. The browser\'s preview URL on AI Studio is `https://ais-dev-27vsgfgocgal3hk7jidvju-794565525699.asia-southeast1.run.app`, and I\'m looking at the discrepancy.\n\n\n**Tracing Root Cause**\n\nI\'m now tracing the root cause of the unexpected HTML response. The `curl` command to `/api/v1/chat` returned a 503, but the browser received HTML. I think I\'ve identified that the server wasn\'t restarted after a recent code edit, meaning `/chat` wasn\'t registered in `apiRouter`. The request then fell through the middleware, leading to the HTML response. I think this explains the error.\n\n\n**Confirming Root Cause**\n\nI\'ve confirmed the root cause of the HTML response: Vite\'s connect middleware, when encountering an unhandled route like `/api/v1/chat`, serves `index.html` with a 200 status, which, when parsed as JSON, results in a `SyntaxError`. This happened because the server hadn\'t been restarted after adding the `/chat` route. Now I\'m focusing on handling `isConfigError` gracefully in `auth.ts` for demo tokens.\n\n\n**Improving Demo Token Handling**\n\nNow, I\'m integrating the proposed improvements. I\'ll modify `auth.ts` to use `DEMO_TOKENS` for a demo user when the database is unconfigured, preventing 503 errors and enabling demo access. In `src/api/routes.ts`, I\'ll update `/auth/session` to return the demo user profile under the same condition. Also, in `POST /chat`, I\'ll ensure `createSeedState().records` are used when no data is found, which provides the assistant with meaningful data. Finally, I\'ll update `apiClient.ts` to reliably handle non-JSON responses from the server, preventing the `SyntaxError`.\n\n\n"
