me back, ...\\\" as the title in manager view, not \\\"Dashboard.\\\" This means I need to adjust the test in `src/test/hackathonFeatures.test.tsx`, specifically line 42. I\'ll change the expected heading to reflect the correct title, resolving the test failure.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/test/hackathonFeatures.test.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"44\",\"StartLine\":\"38\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading hackathonFeatures.test.tsx lines\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read hackathonFeatures.test.tsx\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":199,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:46:29Z\",\"input_tokens\":2805,\"cache_read_tokens\":190605,\"output_tokens\":213,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update test assertion for manager dashboard heading in hackathonFeatures.test.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"43\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Change heading name expectation to /Welcome back/i\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"    expect(await screen.findByRole(\'heading\', { level: 1, name: /Welcome back/i })).toBeInTheDocument();\\\"\",\"StartLine\":\"41\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"    expect(await screen.findByRole(\'heading\', { level: 1, name: \'Dashboard\' })).toBeInTheDocument();\\\"\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/test/hackathonFeatures.test.tsx\\\"\",\"TargetLintErrorIds\":\"[]\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating test assertion\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update hackathonFeatures.test.tsx\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":201,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:46:34Z\",\"input_tokens\":3345,\"cache_read_tokens\":190589,\"output_tokens\":100,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"npx vitest run src/test/hackathonFeatures.test.tsx\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\".\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"10000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Running hackathonFeatures test\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Run hackathonFeatures test\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":203,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:46:44Z\",\"input_tokens\":3783,\"cache_read_tokens\":190575,\"output_tokens\":95,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"compile_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Compiling applet after test fix\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Compile applet\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":205,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:47:12Z\",\"input_tokens\":3972,\"cache_read_tokens\":190563,\"output_tokens\":1132,\"content\":\"### SMARTMESS AI \342\200\224 FINAL HACKATHON DELIVERY REPORT\\n\\nWe have successfully completed all priorities and verified the application codebase, production build, and test suite.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Summary of Completed Priorities & Deliverables\\n\\n1. **Redesigned Login Experience (Priority 1)**:\\n   - Transformed the sign-in page into a polished AI SaaS landing screen featuring a deep navy background (`#0a0f1d`), emerald-green accents, and glowing ambient gradients.\\n   - Added the brand subtitle: *\\\"AI-powered institutional d\\n<truncated 1983 bytes>\\nty 5)**:\\n   - Explicitly disclosed as unconfigured / not connected in settings and status documentation.\\n\\n6. **Build, Test, & Finishing (Priority 6)**:\\n   - **TypeScript Compilation (`tsc --noEmit`)**: PASSED (0 errors).\\n   - **Linting & Production Build (`npm run build`)**: PASSED (Vite production bundle built cleanly).\\n   - **Test Suite (`npx vitest run`)**: All hackathon feature tests, workflow checks, and fallback unit tests passed successfully.\\n   - Updated `TASK_STATUS.md` with complete documentation.\",\"thinking\":\"**Evaluating Implementation Success**\\n\\nI\'m pleased to report a successful build! Now, I\'m carefully reviewing the implementation to ensure it meets every requirement outlined in the user request. So far, the focus is on the crucial redesign of the login experience, where I\'m cross-checking the deep navy background, the emerald-green accents, and the high-contrast text to meet the target requirements.\\n\\n\\n\",\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\"]}\n{\"step_index\":206,\"source\":\"USER_EXPLICIT\",\"type\":\"USER_INPUT\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T18:07:25Z\",\"content\":\"<USER_REQUEST>\\nFix the errors in the app\\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\\nfix_it_trigger: manual\\nerror 0: [AI Assistant] Chat error: SyntaxError: Unexpected token \'<\', \\\"<!doctype \\\"... is not valid JSON\\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]\\n</USER_REQUEST>\\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\\nThe current local time is: 2026-10-20T11:07:25-07:00.\\n\\nModel: models/gemini-3.8-flash\\nDevelopment App URL: https://ais-dev-27vsgfgocgal3hk7jidvju-794565525699.asia-southeast1.run.app\\nShared App URL: https://ais-pre-27vsgfgocgal3hk7jidvju-794565525699.asia-southeast1.run.app\\nUser Email: mahmoodmilhaan777@gmail.com\\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\"}\n{\"step_index\":207,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T18:07:25Z\",\"input_tokens\":196001,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":407,\"thinking\":\"**Addressing the Errors**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on pinpointing and resolving the syntax error within the application. The specific trigger is manual, and it seems the system is encountering an unexpected \\\"<\\\" character within a JSON context, likely in the form of HTML. I\'m prioritizing this critical error to ensure the application\'s stability.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/server.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading server.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read server.ts\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":209,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T18:07:40Z\",\"input_tokens\":3321,\"cache_read_tokens\":193970,\"output_tokens\":255,\"thinking\":\"**Investigating Current Process**\\n\\nI\'ve just been looking at the `package.json` file, and I see the scripts define both a `dev` script using `tsx` and a `start` script using plain `node`. Now I\'m focused on figuring out exactly what server process is currently running within the AI Studio Build dev environment, as that will influence how I should proceed.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/api/routes.ts\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"860\",\"StartLine\":\"840\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking routes.ts for chat route\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check /chat route in routes.ts\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":211,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T18:07:48Z\",\"input_tokens\":2869,\"cache_read_tokens\":195278,\"output_tokens\":122,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/middleware/auth.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading auth middleware\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read auth.ts\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":213,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T18:07:53Z\",\"input_tokens\":4088,\"cache_read_tokens\":196038,\"output_tokens\":552,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Authentication Logic**\\n\\nI\'ve been examining the authentication middleware, specifically focusing on the demo token handling in `src/middleware/auth.ts`, lines 46-60. I\'m trying to understand how demo users are managed and their corresponding user IDs are associated. Currently investigating the error handling within that block.\\n\\n\\n**Investigating Configuration Errors**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into the error handling within the authentication logic, particularly the `isConfigError` check. I see that an unconfigured database results in a 503 error, which seems consistent with the observed behavior. I\'m trying to figure out if that 503 is the cause of the chat error I was experiencing. Next, I\'ll see where `api.sendChatMessage` routes to by checking `apiClient.ts`.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/vite.config.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading vite.config.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read vite.config.ts\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":215,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T18:08:00Z\",\"input_tokens\":3110,\"cache_read_tokens\":198197,\"output_tokens\":159,\"thinking\":\"**Observing Vite\'s Behavior**\\n\\nI\'m focusing intently on Vite\'s behavior in development. I\'m noticing a specific pattern when accessing `/api/v1/chat` in dev mode, particularly when the Vite server is running directly. I need to figure out which script the dev server is using.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"ps aux\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\".\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"2000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking running processes\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check running processes\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":217,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T18:08:06Z\",\"input_tokens\":3394,\"cache_read_tokens\":199269,\"output_tokens\":1021,\"thinking\":\"**Investigating Server Startup**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on the server\'s startup time. I\'ve examined PID 2616 and the commands used, noting the start time of 17:47. I\'m now cross-referencing this against recent code changes, particularly in `server.ts`. This may help me to find potential causes of the issue.\\n\\n\\n**Pinpointing the Root Cause**\\n\\nI\'ve just realized the `tsx server.ts` script in `package.json` lacks the `--watch` flag. This means `server.ts` only runs once, and doesn\'t automatically reload when de\\n<truncated 392 bytes>\\nes in the error handling within `apiClient.ts`. Specifically, I\'m focusing on scenarios where `res.ok` might incorrectly evaluate as true, even when a non-JSON response (like HTML) is returned, such as with a 404 or a 200 HTML response. This leads to a `SyntaxError` when attempting to parse the HTML as JSON. I\'m also cross-checking if the server, with all of its dependencies, needs to be restarted, and if `\\\"dev\\\": \\\"tsx watch server.ts\\\"` in `package.json` should be implemented for automatic server reloads.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"curl -i -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/chat -H \\\\\\\"Content-Type: application/json\\\\\\\" -H \\\\\\\"Authorization: Bearer demo-token-manager\\\\\\\" -d \'{\\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"hello\\\\\\\"}\'\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\".\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"2000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Testing /api/v1/chat endpoint\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Curl /api/v1/chat\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\"]}\n{\"step_index\":219,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T18:08:16Z\",\"input_tokens\":3450,\"cache_read_tokens\":200903,\"output_tokens\":747,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing the auth issue**\\n\\nI\'ve been looking at the curl output, a 503 error, specifically a Service Unavailable error related to an authentication database lookup failure. Now, I\'m focusing on `auth.ts`, specifically lines 46-60, which seems pertinent to handling authenticated demo and test tokens.\\n\\n\\n**Investigating the demo auth**\\n\\nI\'m now zeroing in on the interaction between demo tokens and the database configuration. The `auth.ts` file, lines 46-60, is where the demo token authentication logic resides. Specifically, when Cloud SQL isn\'t configured, the code path hits an unexpected 503 error, even when using demo tokens. It\'s the `isConfigError(error)` that causes it. I\'m trying to understand why this unconfigured database state breaks the demo unexpectedly, considering other parts of the demo appeared to work despite this.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/store/AppStore.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"100\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading AppStore.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read AppStore.tsx\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":221,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T18:08:32Z\",\"input_tokens\":2463,\"cache_read_tokens\":204499,\"output_tokens\":95,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/store/AppStore.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"320\",\"StartLine\":\"250\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading switchRole in AppStore.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read switchRole\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":223,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T18:08:38Z\",\"input_tokens\":3262,\"cache_read_tokens\":204853,\"output_tokens\":3005,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Token Handling**\\n\\nI\'ve been examining the `switchRole` function and its use of fallback tokens. Specifically, I\'m focusing on how `auth.ts` handles those tokens. I\'ve pinpointed the relevant code block within `src/middleware/auth.ts`, the one that explicitly addresses verified demo/test tokens, which has provided additional context to the flow.\\n\\n\\n**Investigating Demo Token Flow**\\n\\nI\'m now diving deeper into how the system verifies and utilizes demo tokens, particularly focusing on the `DEMO_TOKE\\n<truncated 3837 bytes>\\nfy `auth.ts` to use `DEMO_TOKENS` for a demo user when the database is unconfigured, preventing 503 errors and enabling demo access. In `src/api/routes.ts`, I\'ll update `/auth/session` to return the demo user profile under the same condition. Also, in `POST /chat`, I\'ll ensure `createSeedState().records` are used when no data is found, which provides the assistant with meaningful data. Finally, I\'ll update `apiClient.ts` to reliably handle non-JSON responses from the server, preventing the `SyntaxError`.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/middleware/auth.ts\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"76\",\"StartLine\":\"40\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing auth.ts demo token logic\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View auth.ts demo token logic\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\"]}\n{\"step_index\":225,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T18:09:06Z\",\"input_tokens\":3769,\"cache_read_tokens\":209189,\"output_tokens\":793,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Authentication Flow**\\n\\nI\'ve been examining the authentication middleware, specifically lines 49-60 of `src/middleware/auth.ts`. My focus is on understanding the database interaction and error handling within the user retrieval process. I\'m noting potential points where configuration issues could arise and how the system responds. I\'m planning to trace the execution flow during an error condition to map where improvements might lie.\\n\\n\\n**Refining Demo User Fallback**\\n\\nI\'ve just reviewed the demo user fallback logic within the authentication flow. It handles the scenario where Cloud SQL isn\'t configured, gracefully falling back to a synthetic user. I particularly like the role assignment based on the token and the clean separation of this logic. Next, I plan to edit `src/middleware/auth.ts` to implement the fallback strategy, given it aligns well with the existing project principles.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Allow demo token fallback when database is unconfigured in auth middleware\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"61\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Fallback to demo user profile on isConfigError for demo tokens\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"    try {\\\\n      dbUser = await getUserByUid(targetUid);\\\\n    } catch (error: any) {\\\\n      if (isConfigError(error)) {\\\\n        console.warn(\'[Auth] Database unconfigured during demo token verification: falling back to demo user\');\\\\n        const role: U\\n<truncated 720 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"49\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"    try {\\\\n      dbUser = await getUserByUid(targetUid);\\\\n    } catch (error: any) {\\\\n      if (isConfigError(error)) {\\\\n        console.warn(\'[Auth] Database unconfigured during demo token verification\');\\\\n      } else {\\\\n        console.error(\'[Auth] Da\\n<truncated 235 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/middleware/auth.ts\\\"\",\"TargetLintErrorIds\":\"[]\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating auth middleware for demo tokens\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update auth.ts\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":227,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T18:09:13Z\",\"input_tokens\":3420,\"cache_read_tokens\":211009,\"output_tokens\":105,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/api/routes.ts\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"910\",\"StartLine\":\"855\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing chat route data fetching\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View /chat route data fetching\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":229,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T18:09:18Z\",\"input_tokens\":3311,\"cache_read_tokens\":212301,\"output_tokens\":143,\"thinking\":\"**Populating Initial Data**\\n\\nI\'m working on the initial data population within `src/api/routes.ts`. When the `records` array is empty, I plan to import `createSeedState` from `../data/mockData.ts` to initialize both `records` and `itemsList`. I\'ll be looking into `src/data/mockData.ts` to see what is provided.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/data/mockData.ts\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"40\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking mockData.ts export\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check createSeedState in mockData.ts\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":231,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T18:09:23Z\",\"input_tokens\":3094,\"cache_read_tokens\":213575,\"output_tokens\":98,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/data/mockData.ts\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"265\",\"StartLine\":\"230\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking createSeedState export\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check createSeedState export\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":233,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T18:09:30Z\",\"input_tokens\":2899,\"cache_read_tokens\":214549,\"output_tokens\":329,\"thinking\":\"**Defining Initial State**\\n\\nI\'ve got the initial state defined! `createSeedState()` is spitting out `{ menus, records, settings, notifications }`. Inside, each record (`rec`) in the `records` array has its `items`. Those `items` are arrays of `RecordItem` objects. They contain details like `name`, `kgPerPortion`, `suggestedPrep`, and status flags (`approvedPrep`, `prepared`, `consumed`). Now I am focused on the zero-length records case.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/services/apiClient.ts\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"70\",\"StartLine\":\"45\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing request function in apiClient.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View request function in apiClient.ts\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":235,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T18:09:37Z\",\"input_tokens\":2938,\"cache_read_tokens\":215434,\"output_tokens\":1232,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Error Handling**\\n\\nI\'ve been examining the error handling strategy within `src/services/apiClient.ts`, specifically lines 62-68. I\'m focusing on how HTTP errors are currently managed. I\'m noting the fallback to an empty object if `res.json()` fails. I\'m also scrutinizing the error message construction and its potential for improvement.\\n\\n\\n**Refining JSON Handling**\\n\\nI\'m now zeroing in on a critical edge case in `apiClient.ts`. The issue arises when a successful HTTP status (200) serves HTML instea\\n<truncated 161 bytes>\\nt type isn\'t JSON, it will return an error along with the response text, which should improve diagnostics.\\n\\n\\n**Implementing Fallback Logic**\\n\\nI\'m now integrating client-side fallback mechanisms within `AiAssistant.tsx` to enhance robustness. My focus is on gracefully handling scenarios where the API request encounters a network issue or the server endpoint becomes unavailable. I plan to provide the user a more informative message in these cases, instead of a vague error. This also means improving the UX.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Safely validate content-type before parsing JSON in apiClient.ts\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"69\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Check content-type and parse json safely\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"  const contentType = res.headers.get(\'content-type\') || \'\';\\\\n  if (!res.ok) {\\\\n    let message = `HTTP ${res.status}: ${res.statusText}`;\\\\n    if (contentType.includes(\'application/json\')) {\\\\n      const errorBody = await res.json().catch(() => ({}));\\\\n \\n<truncated 347 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"62\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"  if (!res.ok) {\\\\n    const errorBody = await res.json().catch(() => ({}));\\\\n    const message = errorBody.error || `HTTP ${res.status}: ${res.statusText}`;\\\\n    throw new Error(message);\\\\n  }\\\\n\\\\n  return res.json() as Promise<T>;\\\"\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/services/apiClient.ts\\\"\",\"TargetLintErrorIds\":\"[]\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating request function in apiClient.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update apiClient.ts\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":237,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T18:09:49Z\",\"input_tokens\":3816,\"cache_read_tokens\":216493,\"output_tokens\":113,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/api/routes.ts\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"20\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing top imports of routes.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View routes.ts top imports\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":239,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T18:09:54Z\",\"input_tokens\":2802,\"cache_read_tokens\":218187,\"output_tokens\":489,\"thinking\":\"**Adding Seed State Import**\\n\\nI\'ve just added the `createSeedState` import to `src/api/routes.ts` as specified. Specifically, I\'ve incorporated `import { createSeedState } from \'../data/mockData.ts\';` near the top of the file, making it accessible for use later. Now I need to figure out where to apply it within the `POST /chat` route logic. The goal is to seed the records correctly.\\n\\n\\n**Implementing Seed State Logic**\\n\\nI\'ve integrated the seeding logic into both the `/chat` and `/auth/session` routes. Within the `/chat` route, I\'ve checked if there are any existing records. If not, the `createSeedState()` function generates initial records and item lists. For the `/auth/session` route, I handle potential database configuration errors by providing a synthetic demo user in the event the database isn\'t ready. This ensures the application can still function in a demo context.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/api/routes.ts\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"80\",\"StartLine\":\"55\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing auth session route\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View auth session route\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"source\":\"USER_EXPLICIT\",\"type\":\"USER_INPUT\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T18:11:17Z\",\"content\":\"<USER_REQUEST>\\nThere was an unexpected error. Finish what you were doing.\\n</USER_REQUEST>\\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\\nThe current local time is: 2026-10-20T11:11:17-07:00.\\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\"}\n{\"step_index\":242,\"source\":\"USER_EXPLICIT\",\"type\":\"USER_INPUT\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T18:11:56Z\",\"content\":\"<USER_REQUEST>\\ncontinue\\n</USER_REQUEST>\\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\\nThe current local time is: 2026-10-20T11:11:56-07:00.\\n\\nModel: models/gemini-3.5-flash-lite\\nDevelopment App URL: https://ais-dev-27vsgfgocgal3hk7jidvju-794565525699.asia-southeast1.run.app\\nShared App URL: https://ais-pre-27vsgfgocgal3hk7jidvju-794565525699.asia-southeast1.run.app\\nUser Email: mahmoodmilhaan777@gmail.com\\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\"}\n{\"step_index\":243,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T18:11:56Z\",\"input_tokens\":214587,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":316,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing the Error**\\n\\nI\'ve been digging into the error report. It seems we have a \\\"SyntaxError: Unexpected token \'<\'\\\" indicating a problem parsing the API response as JSON. My working hypothesis is that an API request, likely from `/api/v1/chat` or a related endpoint, is failing silently, potentially due to an unhandled exception or server-side error. We need to investigate potential server-side issues.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/api/routes.ts\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"930\",\"StartLine\":\"845\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading chat route in routes.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read /chat route\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":245,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T18:12:05Z\",\"input_tokens\":6731,\"cache_read_tokens\":209815,\"output_tokens\":634,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Database Queries**\\n\\nI\'m currently looking into how other routes manage database interactions, especially when the database (`db`) might throw an error. I\'ve found an example in `src/api/routes.ts` where a `try...catch` block handles database selections.\\n\\n\\n**Refining Error Handling**\\n\\nI\'ve been refining how the `/chat` route handles errors, focusing on ensuring a valid JSON response is always returned. I realized that unhandled server errors, including those triggered by an unconfigured database, could lead to the Vite dev server serving `index.html` instead of JSON. To prevent this, I\'m wrapping the entire `/chat` handler in a `try...catch` block.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/api/routes.ts\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"974\",\"StartLine\":\"848\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading entire /chat route in routes.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read /chat route\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":247,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T18:12:10Z\",\"input_tokens\":9859,\"cache_read_tokens\":209877,\"output_tokens\":288,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Error Handling**\\n\\nI\'ve been examining the error handling, noting inconsistencies. The current code returns JSON for server errors in certain places like lines 968-971, but HTML is returned in others, leading to an inconsistent client experience. There is now a need to ensure a consistent JSON response for all errors from the server.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"curl -i -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/chat -H \\\\\\\"Content-Type: application/json\\\\\\\" -H \\\\\\\"Authorization: Bearer demo-token-manager\\\\\\\" -d \'{\\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"hello\\\\\\\"}\'\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\".\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"2000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Testing chat endpoint with curl\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Test chat endpoint\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":249,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T18:12:15Z\",\"input_tokens\":2208,\"cache_read_tokens\":218317,\"output_tokens\":114,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"compile_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Compiling applet after error fix\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":