  user_input {
    user_response: "Make only the remaining required fixes in the existing SmartMess AI project. Do not redesign unrelated pages or rewrite working features.\n\n1. Ensure the AI Assistant is available only to Mess Manager. Hide its navigation item for Kitchen Staff and Student/Diner, protect the frontend route, and enforce manager-only authorization on POST /api/v1/chat at the backend. Unauthorized requests must return HTTP 403 with a consistent JSON response. Test both UI access and direct API requests for all three roles.\n\n2. Verify that the actual first page visibly uses Design A: institutional dining imagery and product messaging on the left, with demo-role sign-in on the right. If it still shows the old role-card-only layout, implement the redesign in the real login route.\n\n3. Verify the AI Assistant request end to end, including valid JSON responses, the idli-preparation question, and safe fallback when Gemini is unavailable. Never expose API keys.\n\nPreserve all existing functionality. Run the build and relevant tests, inspect the actual rendered preview, and report what was genuinely verified. Do not claim success based on compilation alone."
    items {
      text: "Make only the remaining required fixes in the existing SmartMess AI project. Do not redesign unrelated pages or rewrite working features.\n\n1. Ensure the AI Assistant is available only to Mess Manager. Hide its navigation item for Kitchen Staff and Student/Diner, protect the frontend route, and enforce manager-only authorization on POST /api/v1/chat at the backend. Unauthorized requests must return HTTP 403 with a consistent JSON response. Test both UI access and direct API requests for all three roles.\n\n2. Verify that the actual first page visibly uses Design A: institutional dining imagery and product messaging on the left, with demo-role sign-in on the right. If it still shows the old role-card-only layout, implement the redesign in the real login route.\n\n3. Verify the AI Assistant request end to end, including valid JSON responses, the idli-preparation question, and safe fallback when Gemini is unavailable. Never expose API keys.\n\nPreserve all existing functionality. Run the build and relevant tests, inspect the actual rendered preview, and report what was genuinely verified. Do not claim success based on compilation alone."
