  planner_response {
    response: "I have successfully implemented the genuine desktop split-screen layout (Design A) for the Login page and resolved the student role-access wording.\n\n### Summary of Changes & Verification\n\n1. **Login Page Redesign (`src/pages/Login.tsx`)**:\n   - Replaced the old centered hero layout with a genuine desktop split-screen layout (`lg:grid lg:grid-cols-12`).\n   - **Left Side (~58% width / `lg:col-span-7`)**: Features a full-height institutional commercial kitchen photograph with a dark navy gradient overlay (`bg-gradient-to-t from-[#07111F] via-[#07111F]/85 to-[#07111F]/50`), SmartMess AI branding badge, headline *\"Smarter Kitchens. Happier Campuses.\"*, supporting text, and three compact feature highlights (AI Demand Forecasting, Reduce Food Waste, Better Dining Experience).\n   - **Right Side (~42% width / `lg:col-span-5`)**: Features a distinct, elevated sign-in/demo panel welcoming users with three compact, clearly differentiated demo-role options (Mess Manager, Kitchen Staff, and Student / Diner).\n   - **Role-Access Correction**: Removed the incorrect claim about asking the AI Assistant from the Student/Diner card, replacing it with accurate wording: *\"View published menus, meal timings, and notifications\"*.\n   - **Responsive Behavior**: Automatically adapts from side-by-side split screen on desktop/tablet to stacked vertical layout on mobile, keeping all role choices fully accessible.\n\n2. **Build & Test Results**:\n   - **TypeScript Compilation (`tsc --noEmit`)**: Passed with 0 errors.\n   - **Production Build (`npm run build`)**: Passed successfully.\n   - **Unit & Auth Tests (`vitest`)**: All tests passed successfully (including manager-only AI Assistant authorization, student/kitchen staff 403 enforcement, and AI fallback tests)."
