  user_input {
    user_response: "Make a focused final refinement to the existing SmartMess AI login page. Preserve the current split-screen Design A, all three demo-role options, existing navigation, and all working application features. Do not rebuild the page from scratch.\n\n1. Keep the premium navy/emerald design and dining-hall image.\n2. Preserve the three demo-role entry points for Mess Manager, Kitchen Staff, and Student/Diner. Make their labels and actions clearly communicate that they enter a synthetic-data demo.\n3. Do not add nonfunctional email/password fields. If real authentication is not implemented, keep the demo-role entry flow honest and clear.\n4. Verify the existing session behaviour. If a valid session is intentionally persisted, document how it works. Do not automatically bypass authentication for a real account-based flow, and do not trust a client-side role selection as production-grade authentication.\n5. Replace unsupported claims such as \342\200\234Verified operations runtime\342\200\235 and \342\200\234Enterprise institutional tier\342\200\235 with accurate product messaging unless those claims can be verified.\n6. Improve small-screen responsiveness, keyboard accessibility, focus states, contrast, and card hover/pressed states without adding distracting animation.\n7. Verify that selecting each demo role opens the correct existing dashboard and that role permissions remain enforced by the backend.\n8. Inspect the actual rendered desktop and mobile previews. Run the build and relevant tests, and report any remaining limitations honestly.\n\nMake only changes that are necessary. Preserve the current working login page and do not modify unrelated features."
    items {
      text: "Make a focused final refinement to the existing SmartMess AI login page. Preserve the current split-screen Design A, all three demo-role options, existing navigation, and all working application features. Do not rebuild the page from scratch.\n\n1. Keep the premium navy/emerald design and dining-hall image.\n2. Preserve the three demo-role entry points for Mess Manager, Kitchen Staff, and Student/Diner. Make their labels and actions clearly communicate that they enter a synthetic-data demo.\n3. Do not add nonfunctional email/password fields. If real authentication is not implemented, keep the demo-role entry flow honest and clear.\n4. Verify the existing session behaviour. If a valid session is intentionally persisted, document how it works. Do not automatically bypass authentication for a real account-based flow, and do not trust a client-side role selection as production-grade authentication.\n5. Replace unsupported claims such as \342\200\234Verified operations runtime\342\200\235 and \342\200\234Enterprise institutional tier\342\200\235 with accurate product messaging unless those claims can be verified.\n6. Improve small-screen responsiveness, keyboard accessibility, focus states, contrast, and card hover/pressed states without adding distracting animation.\n7. Verify that selecting each demo role opens the correct existing dashboard and that role permissions remain enforced by the backend.\n8. Inspect the actual rendered desktop and mobile previews. Run the build and relevant tests, and report any remaining limitations honestly.\n\nMake only changes that are necessary. Preserve the current working login page and do not modify unrelated features."
    }
  }
}
