s\":0,\"output_tokens\":382,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing the Error Report**\\n\\nI\'m now zeroing in on the critical database configuration error. It\'s clear that the environment variables (SQL_HOST, SQL_DB_NAME, SQL_USER, SQL_PASSWORD) are missing, which is preventing database persistence. The seed check deferral or non-fatal nature of the second error is noted, though it seems secondary to the database issue. I\'ll need to focus on configuring those .env variables to proceed.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/db/seed.ts\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"100\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading src/db/seed.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read seed.ts\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":334,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T18:26:37Z\",\"input_tokens\":3215,\"cache_read_tokens\":80703,\"output_tokens\":100,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/db/index.ts\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"100\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading src/db/index.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read db/index.ts\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":336,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T18:26:43Z\",\"input_tokens\":2591,\"cache_read_tokens\":82749,\"output_tokens\":98,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/db/index.ts\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"171\",\"StartLine\":\"101\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading src/db/index.ts tail\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read db/index.ts tail\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":338,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T18:26:47Z\",\"input_tokens\":3845,\"cache_read_tokens\":82727,\"output_tokens\":424,\"thinking\":\"**Addressing Database Setup**\\n\\nI\'ve determined that when the database configuration is absent, `db.select()` throws a `DatabaseConfigurationError`. I\'ve started integrating this knowledge into `server.ts`. Currently, I\'m working on seeding the database with a baseline dataset if the tables are empty, and handling potential errors during this seeding process.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/db/seed.ts\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"15\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading seed.ts top\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read seed.ts top\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":340,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T18:26:52Z\",\"input_tokens\":2649,\"cache_read_tokens\":84848,\"output_tokens\":591,\"thinking\":\"**Reviewing Database Seed**\\n\\nI\'m currently reviewing the `seedDatabaseIfEmpty` function in `src/db/seed.ts`. My key focus now is updating it to call `resolveDatabaseConfig()` before proceeding. This should improve robustness by ensuring the database configuration is valid before the seeding process begins. I\'m exploring the implications for error handling and logging as well.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Bypass seedDatabaseIfEmpty when database environment variables are unconfigured\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"14\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Check resolveDatabaseConfig in seedDatabaseIfEmpty and return false if not configured\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"import { eq } from \'drizzle-orm\';\\\\nimport { db, resolveDatabaseConfig } from \'./index\';\\\\nimport { institutions, messes, messSettings, menus, menuItems, mealRecords, recordItems } from \'./schema\';\\\\nimport { createSeedState } from \'../data/mockData\';\\\\n\\\\nimp\\n<truncated 493 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"import { eq } from \'drizzle-orm\';\\\\nimport { db } from \'./index\';\\\\nimport { institutions, messes, messSettings, menus, menuItems, mealRecords, recordItems } from \'./schema\';\\\\nimport { createSeedState } from \'../data/mockData\';\\\\n\\\\nimport { users } from \'./s\\n<truncated 372 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/db/seed.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating seedDatabaseIfEmpty\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update seed.ts\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":342,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T18:26:56Z\",\"input_tokens\":3664,\"cache_read_tokens\":84904,\"output_tokens\":49,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"compile_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Compiling applet after seed update\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Compile applet\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":344,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T18:27:11Z\",\"input_tokens\":3806,\"cache_read_tokens\":84893,\"output_tokens\":55,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"lint_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Linting codebase\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Lint applet\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":346,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T18:27:21Z\",\"input_tokens\":3974,\"cache_read_tokens\":84882,\"output_tokens\":70,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"restart_dev_server\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Restarting dev server\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Restart dev server\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":348,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T18:27:23Z\",\"input_tokens\":4134,\"cache_read_tokens\":84871,\"output_tokens\":154,\"content\":\"I have successfully resolved the startup warnings and database configuration check:\\n\\n1. **Graceful Database Seeding Bypass**:\\n   - Updated `seedDatabaseIfEmpty` to check `resolveDatabaseConfig()` before executing queries. When PostgreSQL / Cloud SQL environment variables (`SQL_HOST`, `SQL_DB_NAME`, `SQL_USER`, `SQL_PASSWORD`) are unconfigured, seeding