    thinking: "**Investigating Database Errors**\n\nI\'ve pinpointed a database configuration error occurring at startup and when routes are accessed. The error log explicitly flags missing environment variables: SQL_HOST, SQL_DB_NAME, SQL_USER, and SQL_PASSWORD. It\'s indicating persistence relies on these .env variables, and they are not configured.\n\n\n**Analyzing Database Connections**\n\nI\'ve traced the root cause of the seeding failure: a missing database connection. Although the seed check deferred, the subsequent Drizzle query via the connection pool in `src/db/index.ts` threw the error. The pool creation itself, through `.connect` or `.query`, checks if the database is configured. The seed script and database connection errors are both connected. This error cascades into Drizzle, throwing the failure.\n\n\n"
