y used, is now missing. I need to understand what this means.\n\n\n**Robustifying Database Configuration**\n\nI\'m now focusing on strengthening the application\'s database configuration handling to prevent the \"Failed query\" error. The issue seems rooted in `resolveDatabaseConfig()` returning `configured: true` even when the PostgreSQL server isn\'t reachable, leading to subsequent Drizzle queries failing. I plan to improve the check to ensure the database connection is truly valid. Specifically, I\'m examining how to make sure that the `seedDatabaseIfEmpty()` function checks the return of `resolveDatabaseConfig()` when the database is unavailable, so that it can seed successfully. This needs to be completely robust across `server.ts`, `seed.ts`, and `index.ts`.\n\n\n"
