    model_api_content_id: "a199807eadd64793b4e6576297dd46a5"
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "# SmartMess AI \342\200\224 Final Submission Fixes Only\n\nContinue in the existing project. Preserve the working UI, manager-only AI access restrictions, role dashboards, approval workflow, notifications, and existing tests. Do not redesign or rewrite working features.\n\n## 1. Fix the invalid Gemini API key\n\nThe current Gemini AI Forecast Insights panel displays HTTP 400 `INVALID_ARGUMENT` with `API_KEY_INVALID`. The AI Assistant also labels at least one response `smartmess-deterministic-fallback`.\n\nInspect the existing server-side Gemini configuration and determine why the forecast-insights request is using an invalid key.\n\n- Verify that the running backend receives `GEMINI_API_KEY` from the server-side Secrets configuration.\n- Confirm that the selected key is intended for the Gemini API and is not empty, stale, or misconfigured.\n- Never print, expose, commit, or return the key.\n- Do not ask me to paste the key into source code or chat.\n- Do not enable billing or create cloud resources without my approval.\n- Perform a real minimal Gemini API request if possible and report the actual result.\n- If the key cannot be fixed within the available environment, keep the deterministic fallback working and explain the exact next configuration step.\n\nMake sure both Forecast Insights and the AI Assistant use the intended server-side configuration consistently, without breaking their separate endpoints.\n\n## 2. Make analytics transparent and trustworthy\n\nInspect the source of the AI Assistant\'s reported metrics: 0 completed services, 450 average attendance, and 0 kg estimated waste.\n\nVerify whether each value is genuinely calculated from available records, a default value, or synthetic demo data.\n\n- Never represent missing records as a verified zero.\n- Distinguish zero recorded waste from unrecorded waste.\n- Label synthetic data clearly.\n- Identify the date range, meal period, and units where relevant.\n- Avoid unsupported profit/loss, waste-reduction, or model-accuracy claims.\n- For preparation questions, use the applicable menu and approved preparation target where available.\n- Clearly label estimates and report missing data instead of inventing quantities.\n\nKeep the manager-only chatbot authorization in both frontend and backend.\n\n## 3. Complete submission documentation\n\nInspect the existing README and submission guide before editing.\n\nEnsure they accurately document:\n- Setup and run instructions for the current project.\n- The three demo roles and how to access them.\n- Synthetic/demo data and current limitations.\n- The rule-based forecasting method, if that is what is implemented.\n- Whether Gemini is connected or fallback mode is active.\n- Any integrations that remain unconfigured.\n\nDo not overwrite useful documentation or claim integrations are live unless verified.\n\n## 4. Final verification\n\nRun the existing build, relevant tests, and API tests. Verify that:\n- The application still launches.\n- All three demo roles work.\n- Student and Kitchen Staff cannot access manager AI analytics.\n- The manager AI chat and Forecast Insights behave correctly.\n- Fallback works when Gemini is unavailable.\n- The approval \342\206\222 kitchen target \342\206\222 student notification workflow remains functional.\n\nCheck the current Git status and commit history to determine whether the latest working changes are present in the intended GitHub repository. Do not push or publish without authorization.\n\nReport the exact results, any remaining configuration steps, and what was genuinely tested. Do not claim live Gemini success unless a real API request succeeds."
    items {
      text: "# SmartMess AI \342\200\224 Final Submission Fixes Only\n\nContinue in the existing project. Preserve the working UI, manager-only AI access restrictions, role dashboards, approval workflow, notifications, and existing tests. Do not redesign or rewrite working features.\n\n## 1. Fix the invalid Gemini API key\n\nThe current Gemini AI Forecast Insights panel displays HTTP 400 `INVALID_ARGUMENT` with `API_KEY_INVALID`. The AI Assistant also labels at least one response `smartmess-deterministic-fallback`.\n\nInspect the existing server-side Gemini configuration and determine why the forecast-insights request is using an invalid key.\n\n- Verify that the running backend receives `GEMINI_API_KEY` from the server-side Secrets configuration.\n- Confirm that the selected key is intended for the Gemini API and is not empty, stale, or misconfigured.\n- Never print, expose, commit, or return the key.\n- Do not ask me to paste the key into source code or chat.\n- Do not enable billing or create cloud resources without my approval.\n- Perform a real minimal Gemini API request if possible and report the actual result.\n- If the key cannot be fixed within the available environment, keep the deterministic fallback working and explain the exact next configuration step.\n\nMake sure both Forecast Insights and the AI Assistant use the intended server-side configuration consistently, without breaking their separate endpoints.\n\n## 2. Make analytics transparent and trustworthy\n\nInspect the source of the AI Assistant\'s reported metrics: 0 completed services, 450 average attendance, and 0 kg estimated waste.\n\nVerify whether each value is genuinely calculated from available records, a default value, or synthetic demo data.\n\n- Never represent missing records as a verified zero.\n- Distinguish zero recorded waste from unrecorded waste.\n- Label synthetic data clearly.\n- Identify the date range, meal period, and units where relevant.\n- Avoid unsupported profit/loss, waste-reduction, or model-accuracy claims.\n- For preparation questions, use the applicable menu and approved preparation target where available.\n- Clearly label estimates and report missing data instead of inventing quantities.\n\nKeep the manager-only chatbot authorization in both frontend and backend.\n\n## 3. Complete submission documentation\n\nInspect the existing README and submission guide before editing.\n\nEnsure they accurately document:\n- Setup and run instructions for the current project.\n- The three demo roles and how to access them.\n- Synthetic/demo data and current limitations.\n- The rule-based forecasting method, if that is what is implemented.\n- Whether Gemini is connected or fallback mode is active.\n- Any integrations that remain unconfigured.\n\nDo not overwrite useful documentation or claim integrations are live unless verified.\n\n## 4. Final verification\n\nRun the existing build, relevant tests, and API tests. Verify that:\n- The application still launches.\n- All three demo roles work.\n- Student and Kitchen Staff cannot access manager AI analytics.\n- The manager AI chat and Forecast Insights behave correctly.\n- Fallback works when Gemini is unavailable.\n- The approval \342\206\222 kitchen target \342\206\222 student notification workflow remains functional.\n\nCheck the current Git status and commit history to determine whether the latest working changes are present in the intended GitHub repository. Do not push or publish without authorization.\n\nReport the exact results, any remaining configuration steps, and what was genuinely tested. Do not claim live Gemini success unless a real API request succeeds."
    }
  }
