  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Seed State Generation**\n\nI\'ve been examining the `createSeedState()` function, and it\'s quite comprehensive! It constructs a 28-day historical data set, plus today\'s meals. I\'m noting the inclusion of `actualDiners`, `predictedDiners`, and detailed `items` data, encompassing preparation and consumption metrics like `prepared`, `consumed`, `kgPerPortion`, and preparation suggestions like `approvedPrep` and `suggestedPrep`. I\'m now turning my attention to the `/chat` endpoint in `src/api/`.\n\n\n**Discovering Route Fallback**\n\nI\'ve discovered an interesting fallback mechanism within `src/api/routes.ts`. When database records are empty, the `/chat` endpoint intelligently leverages `createSeedState()` to populate the dataset. This ensures that the application doesn\'t simply crash when encountering a fresh or empty database. This results in the `/chat` computations having synthetic data to work with, allowing it to provide metrics. It is an interesting solution for initial state population!\n\n\n**Verifying Data Integrity**\n\nI\'m now diving into the `meal` data, specifically focusing on `estimatedTotalWasteKg` and `dataOrigin`. I see \"Synthetic demonstration dataset (reproducible)\" or \"Live PostgreSQL persistence\" flags which is good, and I\'m verifying that the data meets Requirement 2 rules. I am examining the prompt provided to Gemini AI and the fallback responses in `/chat` to check for data integrity. The system prompt is well defined.\n\n\n**Evaluating Data Context**\n\nI am now focusing on the data context metrics. The current total records and completed services are ${dataContext.totalRecords} and ${dataContext.completedRecords}, respectively, for the chosen data origin. The estimated total recorded waste is ${dataContext.estimatedTotalWasteKg} kg, accumulated across completed synthetic services. Average attendance is ${dataContext.averageAttendance} diners per completed service. Top leftover dishes are ${JSON.stringify(topDishes)}. There are ${dataContext.approvedPlansCount} active approved plans. I\'m taking care to clarify the source of these metrics.\n\n\n**Investigating Prompt Responses**\n\nI\'m now examining the conditional logic within the `/chat` endpoint! Specifically, I\'m analyzing the responses generated for queries containing keywords like \"idli\" or \"breakfast\". The system now provides detailed recommendations for batch cooking and suggested prep based on historical attendance, menu portions, and an active approved plan. It also details waste based on the data origin.\n\n\n**Checking UI Integration**\n\nI\'m now investigating the user interface, specifically the Manager Analytics dashboard. I\'m verifying that the attendance and preparation plan metrics I previously analyzed are accurately displayed and aligned with the backend data. I\'m also looking for any visualizations or data presentation styles.\n\n\n"
