  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining `/chat` Route**\n\nI\'m currently focusing on the `/chat` route within `src/api/routes.ts`, specifically lines 1040-1160. My primary concern is ensuring the `/chat` endpoint defaults to seed data if the database lacks relevant records or configuration. This is crucial for maintaining the integrity of our 28-day synthetic baseline dataset used for metric calculations, preventing unwanted defaults.\n\n\n**Analyzing POST /chat**\n\nI\'ve been reviewing the `POST /chat` route within `src/api/routes.ts`, focusing on how it handles database retrieval. I\'m satisfied that it correctly defaults to seed data when no records are found, ensuring the synthetic 28-day baseline is used. The code accurately determines and indicates if synthetic data is used. I\'ve specifically examined lines 1040-1060 and 1060-1075, as well as the logic from 1075 through 1090.\n\n\n**Calculating Waste Metrics**\n\nI\'m currently delving into the waste calculation logic. I\'ve broken down the calculation of `totalWasteKg` based on `consumed`, `leftover`, and `kgPerPortion`. Then, I\'m tracking the leftovers per dish using a `dishLeftovers` map to sum the waste and get the total in kg, and this is then used to create `topDishes`, the top 5 most wasted dishes. I am now looking at average attendance calculations. I am ensuring that I handle possible null and zero cases appropriately for the `avgAttendance` calculation. Finally, I\'ve got data context variables for reporting.\n\n\n**Reviewing Metric Reporting**\n\nI\'m now satisfied with the data context variables used for reporting. I am pleased with the generated fallback and Gemini replies. The response accurately reflects the data from the reproducible synthetic dataset. I\'m focusing on the clarity and accuracy of the reporting regarding estimated waste and top dishes. I will ensure this data is presented concisely and understandably. The context confirms the 87 records, the 85 completed meals, average attendance, and the estimated total waste.\n\n\n"
