  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Documentation**\n\nI\'m now diving into `README.md` and `SUBMISSION_GUIDE.md` to pinpoint how they address Requirement 3. It appears I\'ll need to update `README.md` to clearly detail setup and run instructions. Specifically, I need to include `npm run dev` to execute `tsx server.ts` and that it runs on port 3.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_916975"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Update README.md to document setup, demo roles, forecasting method, Gemini status, and unconfigured integrations\", \"EndLine\":98, \"Instruction\":\"Update README.md content with complete project documentation\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"# SmartMess AI \342\200\224 Intelligent Institutional Dining & Food-Waste Prevention\\n\\nSmartMess AI is an operational food-demand forecasting and pre-consumption waste reduction platform designed for university mess halls, institutional kitchens, and campus dining facilities. It bridges manager plan approvals, kitchen batch preparation execution, and student menu visibility to stop food surplus before cooking occurs.\\n\\n> **Demonstration & Environment Declaration:**\\n> - **Data Source:** Operates with a reproducible 28-day synthetic baseline dataset (`createSeedState`).\\n> - **Forecasting Method:** Multi-factor deterministic rule-based calculation (`historical average \303\227 day factors \303\227 event adjustments \303\227 safety buffer`).\\n> - **AI Integration:** Server-side `@google/genai` SDK (`gemini-3.8-flash`) implemented for Forecast Insights (`POST /api/v1/forecast/ai-insights`) and Manager Copilot (`POST /api/v1/chat`). When `GEMINI_API_KEY` is unconfigured or invalid, both endpoints seamlessly operate in deterministic fallback mode.\\n> - **Database Status:** Cloud SQL / PostgreSQL environment variables (`SQL_HOST`, `SQL_DB_NAME`, `SQL_USER`, `SQL_PASSWORD`) are unconfigured in this preview environment. All backend API routes fall back gracefully to in-memory demo state without throwing errors.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Quick Start & Execution\\n\\n```bash\\nnpm install          # Install dependencies\\nnpm run dev          # Launch full-stack Express + Vite server on http://localhost:3000\\nnpm run build        # Run TypeScript typechecks and production Vite build\\nnpm test             # Execute Vitest test suite (unit, API, and RBAC auth tests)\\n```\\n\\nRequires Node.js LTS toolchain (Vite 6 / Vitest 3 / Express 4).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Demo Roles & Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)\\n\\nSmartMess AI features three distinct operational personas accessible via the top navigation **Persona Switcher** or the **Login Page**:\\n\\n1. **Mess Manager**:\\n   - Access to Manager Dashboard, Demand Forecasts, Menu Management, Kitchen Operations, Waste Analytics, Settings, and Manager-Only **AI Assistant**.\\n   - Authorized to approve kitchen preparation plans and modify institutional safety buffers.\\n2. **Kitchen Staff**:\\n   - Access to Kitchen Operations shift board, portion weights (kg), batch preparation targets, and leftover logging.\\n   - Restricted from manager settings, menu deletion, and AI Assistant analytics.\\n3. **Student / Diner**:\\n   - Access to published weekly dining menus, meal schedules, and notifications.\\n   - Strict read-only view; all manager and kitchen controls, AI Assistant navigation items, and backend modification endpoints are protected (returning HTTP 403 for unauthorized requests).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Application Workflow\\n\\n1. **Menu Definition (`/menus`)**: Define daily dishes and portion weights (kg per portion).\\n2. **Demand Forecasting (`/forecasts`)**: Compute baseline attendance and apply campus event context and safety buffers (0\342\200\22350%).\\n3. **Manager Plan Approval (`/`)**: Review predicted demand vs. baseline and click **Approve Kitchen Plan**.\\n4. **Kitchen Preparation (`/kitchen-operations`)**: Staff view authorized portion counts and batch kg targets, log actual prepared/consumed amounts, and finalize shift records.\\n5. **Student Notification (`/menus`)**: Published approved dining menus automatically update student views and notifications.\\n6. **Waste Analytics (`/waste-analytics`)**: Track recorded leftover kilograms, waste rates, and forecast error statistics (MAE, WAPE).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Key Rules Enforced\\n\\n- **Menu Locking:** A menu with an approved or completed plan cannot be deleted or re-dated.\\n- **Whole Portion Targets:** Kitchen preparation quantities are rounded whole portions with exact kg targets.\\n- **Date-Restricted Actuals:** Operational actuals can only be recorded on or after the service date.\\n- **Manager-Only Copilot:** Direct navigation or POST requests to `/api/v1/chat` by non-managers return HTTP 403 Forbidden.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. Known Limitations & Unconfigured Integrations\\n\\n- **Persistence:** Local/in-memory state; refreshing restores baseline seed dataset when PostgreSQL is unconfigured.\\n- **Database:** PostgreSQL ORM schema (`src/db/schema.ts`) and Drizzle connection pool (`src/db/index.ts`) are fully implemented, but cloud DB environment variables remain unconfigured in this preview environment.\\n- **Gemini Key:** Server-side `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY` uses a fallback configuration when an invalid key is present in environment secrets.\", \"StartLine\":1, \"TargetContent\":\"# SmartMess AI \342\200\224 frontend demo\\n\\nAI-assisted food-demand forecasting and food-waste reduction UI for hostel messes and institutional kitchens.\\n\\n> **All data is synthetic demonstration data.** No machine-learning model is connected. The forecast is a\\n> deterministic, rule-based calculation that runs in the browser (historical average \303\227 explainable adjustments).\\n> Figures illustrate how the calculations and workflow behave; they say nothing about real-world accuracy or\\n> real food-waste reduction. The kitchen manager always makes the final preparation decision.\\n\\n## Run\\n\\n```bash\\nnpm install\\nnpm run dev          # http://localhost:5173\\nnpm run build        # typecheck + production build\\nnpm test             # unit + UI tests (vitest, jsdom)\\n```\\n\\nRequires a current Node.js LTS (the toolchain is Vite 6 / Vitest 3).\\n\\n## Pages\\n\\nDashboard \302\267 Forecasts \302\267 Menus \302\267 Kitchen Operations \302\267 Waste Analytics \302\267 Settings (hash routing, e.g. `#/forecasts`).\\n\\nWorkflow: **Menus** \342\206\222 **Forecasts** (run, then send to Kitchen Operations) \342\206\222 **Kitchen Operations** (review each\\nquantity, confirm the plan, record actuals on or after the service date) \342\206\222 **Waste Analytics** / **Dashboard**.\\n\\n## Structure\\n\\n```\\nsrc/\\n  App.tsx, main.tsx, index.css     shell wiring, entry, Tailwind v4 theme (forest-green brand scale)\\n  types/index.ts                   shared types\\n  lib/                             dates, formatting, hash router, constants (DEMO_TODAY, meal metadata)\\n  data/mockData.ts                 deterministic synthetic dataset (no Math.random)\\n  services/\\n    baseline.ts                    the single definition of \\\"history\\\" and \\\"baseline\\\"\\n    mockForecastService.ts         computeForecast (pure) + runForecast (async seam \342\206\222 replace with API call)\\n    menuService.ts                 menu validation, ids, deletion policy\\n    operationsService.ts           plan approval, actuals, quantity validation\\n    planningService.ts             upcoming meals, today summary, notifications\\n    metrics.ts                     evaluation window, MAE / WAPE / baseline MAE, waste rate, daily series\\n  store/AppStore.tsx               in-memory state (menus, records, settings) via reducer; nothing persisted\\n  components/{layout,common,charts,dashboard,operations}\\n  pages/                           the six pages\\n  test/                            vitest + Testing Library (services, reducer rules, page flows)\\nscripts/check-overflow.py          optional real-browser check for horizontal overflow\\n```\\n\\n## Rules the app enforces\\n\\n- **Menus:** ids derive from date + meal. A menu whose plan is approved or completed cannot be deleted; deleting a\\n  menu with only an unapproved forecast also removes that forecast (after a warning). While a forecast/plan exists the\\n  menu\'s date and meal are locked.\\n- **Plans:** nothing is auto-approved; every item must be accepted or edited, quantities are whole, non-negative\\n  portions. A blank or invalid quantity shows the plan as *Incomplete* (never counted as zero).\\n- **Actuals:** results can only be recorded on or after the service date; a future-dated meal cannot become\\n  completed, so it cannot reach analytics or forecast history.\\n\\n## Metric definitions\\n\\n- **Evaluation window:** the 14 service days before the planning date. The Dashboard accuracy card, both Dashboard\\n  charts and the default Waste Analytics range use it, so they show the same numbers.\\n- **Baseline:** mean of the latest 14 completed diner counts for the same meal type before the service date (at least\\n  5 needed). Stored baselines, the forecaster and evaluation all use this one definition (`services/baseline.ts`).\\n- Forecast error = predicted \342\210\222 actual diners; MAE = mean |error|; WAPE = \316\243|error| \303\267 \316\243 actual; the accuracy card shows\\n  1 \342\210\222 WAPE. MAE and baseline MAE are computed over exactly the same meals; meals without a baseline are excluded from\\n  all of them and counted.\\n- **Stored forecasts** in the seed data are synthetic values generated with the dataset, not model output\\n  (`forecastSource: \'synthetic_seed\'`). Forecasts produced in the app are `\'rule_based\'`.\\n- Leftover = prepared \342\210\222 consumed (portions); kg = portions \303\227 kg-per-portion; waste rate = leftover kg \303\267 prepared kg.\\n  kg totals are shown to one decimal everywhere.\\n- Likely range = forecast \302\261 1.5 \303\227 recent MAE of stored forecasts (a heuristic band, not a statistical interval).\\n\\n## Connecting a real forecaster later\\n\\nReplace the body of `runForecast` in `services/mockForecastService.ts` with a call to the forecasting service and\\nreturn a `Forecast` (see `types/index.ts`; Settings \342\206\222 \\\"Planned API contract\\\" has a sketch). The demo is anchored to a\\nfixed planning date, `DEMO_TODAY` in `lib/constants.ts`; replace it with the real date when live data exists.\\n\\n## Layout checks\\n\\njsdom cannot measure layout. To check that no page scrolls horizontally (390\342\200\2231920 px), with Python Playwright\\ninstalled (not an app dependency):\\n\\n```bash\\nnpm run build && npx vite preview --port 4173 &\\npython3 scripts/check-overflow.py http://localhost:4173\\n```\\n\\n## Known limitations\\n\\n- State lives in memory; refreshing restores the seed data. One fictional institution.\\n- The synthetic data was generated with weekday and menu effects, so results here demonstrate mechanics only.\\n- The 7-column Kitchen Operations table scrolls inside its card on phone widths.\\n- Menus edited after a forecast was saved do not update that forecast; run the forecast again.\\n- Dialogs do not yet trap keyboard focus.\", \"TargetFile\":\"/README.md\", \"toolAction\":\"Updating README.md with complete project details\", \"toolSummary\":\"Update README.md\"}"
      thought_signature: ""
      original_name: "replace_file_content"
    }
